# Cache policy for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Cloudflare applies every matching block in file order and JOINS repeated
# headers with a comma. For Cache-Control that is not a merge, it is a
# contradiction: `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000,
# immutable` is one header holding two max-age values, and RFC 9111 leaves the
# outcome to the cache. Nothing errors and the asset still serves, which is
# exactly what makes it worth writing carefully.
#
# So the two policies here do not sit side by side hoping order saves them. The
# broad block comes first, and the narrow one DETACHES the header before
# setting its own: `! Cache-Control` removes what earlier blocks added, which is
# the documented way for a narrower rule to win. The `!` line is
# Cloudflare-specific and does nothing on Netlify — this file is written for
# Cloudflare Pages.
#
#   /*          every page: revalidate, so a deploy is visible at once
#   /404.html   no-store, because it is served for arbitrary wrong URLs
#   /assets/*   one year, immutable, because every URL carries ?v=<hash>
#
# The immutable claim is only true while assets stay versioned. _assets.cjs
# hashes the file bytes into ?v=, and the generators call it for everything
# they emit: stylesheet, scripts, data files, the brand mark, gift photos, the
# per-locale runtime bundles. Editing a file changes its URL, so a year-long
# cache can never pin an old build. _check_assets_versioned.cjs is the guard —
# run it before deploying, and a bare /assets/ path fails there instead of
# silently freezing in visitors' browsers.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# A 404 is served for whatever URL the visitor mistyped, so it must never be
# stored: after a deploy changes the links in that page, the next visitor
# should get the new ones rather than a copy from their disk.
/404.html
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-store

# The year-long rule. Safe only because the URL is the cache key: a changed
# file has a changed URL, so nothing ever needs to be revalidated in place.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
